{"name":"Delicate Snow Goose","hex":"#d1e2d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"snow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The partly frozen, crystalline state of water that falls from the atmosphere as precipitation in flakes; also, the falling of such flakes; and the accumulation of them on the ground or on objects as a white layer.\n\n An instance of the falling of snow (etymology 1, noun sense 1); a snowfall; also, a snowstorm.","An instance of the falling of snow (etymology 1, noun sense 1); a snowfall; also, a snowstorm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Preceded by the dummy subject it: to have snow (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1) fall from the atmosphere.","Of a thing: to fall like snow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snow"},{"term":"goose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grazing waterfowl of the family Anatidae, which have feathers and webbed feet and are capable of flying, swimming, and walking on land, and which are generally bigger than ducks.","A female goose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sharply poke or pinch the buttocks, or prod between the buttocks (of a person).","To stimulate; to spur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snow goose","blocks":[{"text":"The snow goose is a species of goose native to North America. Both white and dark morphs exist, the latter often known as blue goose. Its name derives from the typically white plumage. The species was previously placed in the genus Chen, but is now typically included in the \"gray goose\" genus Anser."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Snow_goose_in_Central_Park_%2833138%29.jpg/330px-Snow_goose_in_Central_Park_%2833138%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_goose"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow"},{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose"},{"title":"Shades of white","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of white are colors that differ slightly from the CIE standard illuminant D65, a white point that represents the average color of daylight at noon. There isn't one objectively pure white, as noon daylight varies by location and atmospheric conditions, and the choice of using D65 instead of direct sunlight or a white point on the Planckian locus is arbitrary. For simplicity, this article will use the term pure white for the D65 white point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Color_icon_white.svg/330px-Color_icon_white.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_white"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Lesser.snow.goose.blue.arp.600pix.jpg/500px-Lesser.snow.goose.blue.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Lesser.snow.goose.blue.arp.600pix.jpg/500px-Lesser.snow.goose.blue.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALesser.snow.goose.blue.arp.600pix.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg/500px-Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg/1280px-Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg/500px-Snow_goose_taking_off_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snow goose at the Gray Lodge Wildlife Area in Northern California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or